# Fineage delivery

## Workspace

- Work in **`/Users/nikitarakitin/Projects/Fineage`** and **`/Users/nikitarakitin/Projects/Fineage-Backend`**.
- Do not create sibling worktrees (`Fineage-net`, etc.) unless the user asks for parallel agents.

## Models

- **Architecture / complex design / epic planning / boundary decisions:** use a **powerful** model (Claude Opus / high-thinking). Do not design the system on Composer alone.
- **Implementation / mechanical coding / tests / CI after design is clear:** use **Composer** (default coding agent). Omit heavy models for hammering.

## Refactor before features

- Prefer **epic #131** (client architecture) progress before **epic #129** (Gremlin smoke) client-heavy work.
- Do not ship Gremlin feature layers onto an unreformed monolith when the change belongs in the arch epic first.

## CI and landing

- Target branch for client feature work: **`dev`** via PR only. Never push to `main`/`dev`.
- Backend: PR into **`dev`** (`main` is protected deploy). Never push to protected defaults directly.
- **Green GitHub Actions** before merge. Fix red CI on the PR branch.

